# refused-precedence — an actor with no authorizing grant yields `refused` (default-deny,
# specification Verdicts). refused pre-empts reserved (g2), prohibited pre-empts refused (g3),
# for an unauthorized actor. Pins runtime refused/prohibited, which Conformance names but no
# other transport produces.
actor a
actor b
gate g1 risk low grant a
gate g2 risk low grant a
gate g3 risk low grant a
reserve sensitive by legal
prohibit forbidden
cord a -> g1
cord a -> g2
cord a -> g3
cord g1 -> master
cord g2 -> master
cord g3 -> master
